</ref>|VRMD<ref name="Chart"/>}} is a [[domestic airport]] located on the island of [[Dharavandhoo]], part of the [[Baa Atoll]] in [[Maldives]]. It was opened on 17 October 2012 by President [[Mohamed Waheed Hassan]].<ref>{{cite news | url = http://www.haveeru.com.mv/news/45124 | title = President opens Dharavandhoo airport | work = [[Haveeru Daily]] | date = 17 October 2012 | access-date = 17 October 2012 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20151002121208/http://www.haveeru.com.mv/news/45124 | archive-date = 2 October 2015 | url-status = dead }}</ref> Flight operations began to the airport on 15th of that month.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://maldives.net.mv/7379/maldivian-begins-scheduled-flights-to-dharavandhoo-airport/ | title = Maldivian begins scheduled flights to Dharavandhoo Airport | publisher = maldives.net.mv | date = 15 October 2012}}</ref>

==Facilities==
The airport resides at an [[elevation]] of {{convert|6|ft|0}} above [[mean sea level]].<ref name="Chart" /> It has one [[runway]] which is {{convert|1189|m|0}} in length.<ref name="Chart" />

